{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader</b> — the sense of \"servant of YHWH\" is that he guards His ways, as in: \"I have kept the ways of YHWH; let YHWH recompense me according to my righteousness.\" And this song was composed when he adjured his men not to go with him to battle anymore, and he mentioned Saul together with his enemies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:29.068183816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}